{
  "version": 1,
  "operation": "SdpaBackward",
  "description": "SDPA backward on packed (THD) ragged tensors over hipkernel:flydsl_sdpa_bwd_split (COVERAGE.md 9.1 PV-3, SS-4, SS-5; 9.3 gap rows): Q, K, V, O, dO, dQ, dK, dV and the LSE are ragged, each with its own INT32 [B + 1, 1, 1, 1] element-offset tensor and the seq_len_q / seq_len_kv tensors, as the SdpaBackward/Golden/Ragged bundles declare them (the template is theirs: its tensors are not numbered canonically, so a failure of this space cannot be frozen into a regression bundle by import_graph.py; BSHD strides, LSE packed (T, H)). Batch entry i has valid lengths max(1, Sq - i * pad_q) and max(1, Skv - i * pad_kv); `gaps` packs the sequences back to back (compact) or leaves each in its padded slot (gapped, so gap rows exist between sequences). All offsets and lengths are exact `values` fills (metadata format 2). O and the LSE come from the harness's ragged forward derivation; the references run the dense padded rewrite. Masks none and causal; no bias, dropout or window with ragged (declined by the matcher or not modelled).",
